Patch 28 -- remove the dead visibility-cull AABB cache from d3d8.

Measured on the device 2026-08-12 with the only build that still carries the
counters, d3d8_producer_batch20_visibilitycull.dll:

    MGS2CULL: frames=300 tested=112800 376.00/f culled=33297 110.99/f
              cache_hit=0 cache_miss=112800

Zero hits in 112,800 lookups, and it cannot be otherwise: the cache key includes
mgs2_geometry_generation, which is bumped on every writable Unlock, and MGS2
re-uploads its dynamic vertex buffers every frame -- the reason the cached
DISCARD shadow of patch 26 exists at all. No entry can survive to its next
lookup, so the cache paid one hash plus up to four key comparisons per tested
draw and 73,760 bytes of BSS for nothing.

Removing it cannot change any culling decision: on a miss the old code computed
the AABB with exactly this loop, and there were only misses.

Measured effect on the stripped production DLL:

    .bss   74,464 -> 704 bytes   (-73,760)
    .text  52,368 -> 51,520      (-848)

Frame rate effect not measured: the available windows came from attract-mode
scenes, and rule 3 of this project forbids reading an A/B off unequal scenes.
The change only removes work, so no regression is expected; a fixed-spot pair of
windows would settle it.
